<p>In the latest development in the Iran-Israel war, Iran&#x27;s Supreme National Security Council and state media confirmed that Ali Larijani, the council&#x27;s secretary and one of the country&#x27;s most influential political figures, was killed in an airstrike that Israel said it carried out in Tehran. Multiple reports said Larijani&#x27;s son and security personnel were also killed, and Iran separately confirmed the death of Basij commander Gholamreza Soleimani in the same wave of strikes. Larijani&#x27;s death matters because he had become a central power broker after the killing of Supreme Leader Ali Khamenei in the first phase of the war on February 28. Several outlets described him as Iran&#x27;s de facto political leader, or at least one of the top figures still shaping security and foreign policy. His killing also appears to narrow the immediate diplomatic space: Iran vowed retaliation and launched missile attacks toward Israel, while Bahrain, Qatar, the UAE, and Saudi Arabia intercepted missiles and drones crossing the Gulf, underscoring how quickly the conflict is spilling across borders.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/_Th78494nsNUnwwJJasfSzxapO0nXt8VxI0EJrMYzB6zHIwFoNHpTOZPHng_8MID8v45Rjht0iX74kOwh4xZPelqOoCZcPjD5RFfBMOmoU5vaWY2WXu9ur_ELV8svEYFlnaA_TrfNQitX-oWDlNR8x4z5gRKudC3WIPc6PVRB7FbI4yPW2Rn7m18jOeqWid0G_94l56gaA7aSKYYf6plVbf3nqjWTQjtHf2iSC5C23GCqd4mxZSNtUK4kBh9vaU0ZeijmjdzNhPeR3KrqA' alt='File photo of Ali Larijani arriving for a meeting in Beirut on Aug. 13, 2025.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>External channel: The Guardian and El País said Larijani&#x27;s importance went beyond his formal role; he was one of the few Iranian insiders with enough stature to deal credibly with foreign powers such as China and Russia in a crisis.</li><li>Hard-line shift: Analysts told the New York Times and Al-Monitor that Larijani had served as a bridge between military hard-liners and more pragmatic factions, so his death could leave the IRGC and other hard-line actors with greater sway over security and foreign policy.</li><li>Domestic record: Several profiles note that while Larijani was sometimes seen as pragmatic in diplomacy, he was also linked to the state&#x27;s crackdown on mass protests in January, a role that drew US sanctions last month.</li><li>Strike significance: Multiple reports described Larijani as the most senior Iranian figure killed since Khamenei, underscoring that Israel&#x27;s campaign is still aimed at the political core of the system, not just battlefield commanders.</li></ul><blockquote>Iran’s response to the assassination of the secretary of the Supreme National Security Council will be decisive and regrettable - Amir Hatami</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Israeli government: Israeli Defense Minister Israel Katz said Larijani and Basij commander Gholamreza Soleimani had been &#x27;eliminated,&#x27; presenting the strike as part of Israel&#x27;s campaign against Iran&#x27;s wartime leadership. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c24deezq6meo'>BBC</a>)</li><li>Iranian leadership: Iran&#x27;s Supreme National Security Council praised Larijani after his death and framed the killing as martyrdom, while military leaders promised a forceful response instead of a ceasefire. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/17/irans-security-chief-ali-larijani-killed-in-airstrike-israel-says'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Regional analysts: Analysts interviewed by PBS said Larijani&#x27;s role in Iran&#x27;s system made his death significant, but they also questioned whether killing senior officials would, by itself, collapse the state or end the war. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/middle-east-analysts-assess-irans-power-structure-after-killing-of-top-official'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>Iranian civilians: The Christian Science Monitor described many Iranians as feeling trapped between continued external attack and an unyielding domestic system, with Larijani&#x27;s killing adding to the sense of crisis rather than bringing clarity. (<a href='https://www.csmonitor.com/World/Middle-East/2026/0317/iranian-war-mood-feeling-trapped'>The Christian Science Monitor</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/635365-iran-confirms-larijani-death/'>Iran confirms death of top security official Ali Larijani in US-Israeli strikes</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/17/irans-security-chief-ali-larijani-killed-in-airstrike-israel-says'>Iran’s national security council confirms death of its chief, Ali Larijani</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/who-was-ali-larijani-iran-s-unofficial-strongman/a-76202526'>Who was Ali Larijani, Iran&#x27;s unofficial strongman?</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://novaramedia.com/2026/03/17/irans-de-facto-leader-killed-israels-war-plan-explained/'>Iran’s De-Facto Leader Killed; Israel’s War Plan Explained</a> - novaramedia.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/iran-vows-revenge-for-security-chief-larijanis-killing-hits-tel-aviv-with-cluster-bombs'>Iran vows revenge for security chief Larijani’s killing, hits Tel Aviv with cluster bombs</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reddit.com/r/worldnews/comments/1rwk1e3/iran_confirms_security_chief_ali_larijani_killed/'>Iran confirms security chief Ali Larijani killed, Iranian media reports</a> - reddit.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-iran-war-israel-strike-ali-larijani-gholam-reza-soleimani-killed/'>Who were Ali Larijani and Gholam Reza Soleimani, the Iranian leaders killed by Israel?</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2026-03-17-0700/middle-east-death-influential-ali-larijani-would-be-bigger-loss-iran-khamenei'>Death of influential Ali Larijani would be bigger loss to Iran than Khamenei</a> - allsides.com</li><li><a href='https://english.elpais.com/internatio